# Variable NAMES only. Never a value — not a placeholder that looks real, not a
# development key, not a "safe" one. This file is tracked; anything written here
# is published.
#
# Real values live in two places: Vercel, where every one is created as
# Sensitive, and an untracked `.env.local` on the maintainer's machine. The
# rules are in .claude/context/security-auth.md; the list below is kept beside
# the decisions that introduce each variable, in .claude/context/backend.md.
#
# No code reads any of these yet. `GET /api/health`, the only route as of plan
# batch 4.2, reads no secret at all — it reports the deployment's commit and
# region from Vercel's own public system variables.
#
# Present on the maintainer's machine since plan batch 5.0, which linked the
# Neon project. The Neon CLI owns these three lines in `.env.local` — both
# `neon deploy` and `neon env pull` rewrite them — but it merges rather than
# replaces, so every other line in that file survives. The Phase 5 names below
# are therefore hand-written into the same file when their batch arrives.
# Nothing imports any of them until batch 5.1 adds the database client:
#   DATABASE_URL
#   DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED
#   NEON_BRANCH             # which Neon branch the two values above point at
#
# Arriving in Phase 5 (sign-in):
#   BETTER_AUTH_SECRET
#   BETTER_AUTH_URL
#   GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID
#   GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET
#   ALLOWED_EMAILS
#   AUTH_TEST_MODE          # local only, never set on a deployment
